Adam thank you so much for joining us  it's great to have you here thanks for  having me  so aside from being here and doing this  interview how is your job different now  that you're CEO oh well we made a couple  of changes over the last quarter and one  of the things that I've done is  inherited some numerous possibilities  we brought the revenue product team  closer to my team and also the media  team but in general look I'm having the  time of my life that the product and the  business are going really well now we  have to start with user growth because  by one metric you lost 2 million core  users then jack says well it's actually  ticking back up what's actually  happening right now with user growth  yeah so what's actually happening right  now is that our user growth in January  has bounced back to our original levels  and we're confident actually in the  product work that we have ahead and that  product work will drive user growth to  you know a sustained period of growth  for the long term if we if we execute  the product changes that we put in place  already in fact we made one yesterday  where you can turn on a simple switch  and get the best of Twitter in your  timeline we think things like that while  small we'll continue to refine what's an  iconic product you say a sustained  period of growth how confident are you  give us a confidence check how confident  are you that you can re accelerate user  growth oh we're confident in the product  roadmap and we're confident in the  trends that we're actually seeing and  some of the trends actually are already  good signs that we talked about in in  earrings call yesterday are da you for  example in terms of as a percentage of  da you daily active users - monthly  active users actually went up for this  past quarter so the signs are there for  sure  but make no make no mistake product  execution ultimately will drive user  growth we feel like we've got a great  product roadmap and we're confident in  the road ahead how confident are you in  Jack Dorsey who has another full-time  job yes so you know jack talked about  his ability to manage both jobs on the  earnings call yesterday I can only speak  from my point of view I've seen him in  action and from a product standpoint  he's unbelievable with the tea  he's got a vision for the company and  you know I'm fascinated by him and his  ability to execute at the company and  he's doing a great job now you live and  breathe Twitter you built the revenue  engine for this company how do you deal  with the the sort of incessant  negativity that surrounds the company  and how is it impacting morale I mean we  know a lot of people have left we know  more people are looking yeah look I  think the morale of the company there's  a massive set of determination at the  company to prove the outside world wrong  and look we heard this on the business  side two five and a half years ago when  we started the business the question was  hey how are they going to monetize the  business if you look at 2015 we had a  really strong 2015 in terms of revenue  growth close to 60 percent year-on-year  growth for 2015 in q4 for this past  quarter what we just announced was  revenue that was over 50% on a constant  currency-based basis so there were  questions about our ability to monetize  we've proven them wrong over the last  five and a half years and I look at the  next five and a half years is a great  chance to prove them wrong again on that  note though revenue growth is slowing  down and guidance suggests upward into  40 percent it was forty eight percent  last quarter revenue growth seems to be  slowing dramatically what's going to  turn that around let me talk a little  bit about what's happening in the  business you know in our revenue stream  on the advertising side we have two  categories of advertisers there's big  branded advertisers so these are people  for example that run TV commercials and  the like and then we have smaller  performance advertisers these people  looking for clicks and conversions and  mostly with inside of digital spend the  brand advertisers business is the  largest percentage of our business and  the growth there since we've covered  most of those advertisers the growth  there is gonna come from just growth and  budgets although we're growing nicely we  just launched video advertising for  example on Twitter and that's growing  budgets the performance business is a  small is a smaller set of our advertiser  revenue but it is extremely fast-growing  and ultimately we have a product driven  approach ahead to drive that revenue  schedule that's the business that people  are concerned about direct response  advertising  why are you having trouble with well  it's not that we're having trouble we  started with the branded advertising  business first and this was the this was  the thing when we looked at five and a  half years ago in terms of the business  and the big brand advertisers were  already on the platform and so we didn't  have to Pied Piper them to the platform  we knew that if we could just make it  easier for them to expand business on  Twitter it would be successful we saw it  this past weekend during the Superbowl  during the Superbowl 90% of the  television advertisers were also running  ads on Twitter and over fifty percent of  that budget was actually running with  instead of our video platform as well  why don't you create a model where the  best content creators can share revenue  from Promoted Tweets I mean if if this  is a social platform for creative  creators and users why not make it a  money-making opportunity for them it  worked for Google it's a great idea and  it's actually something we've already  started so Jack talked a little bit  about one of the key priorities for us  was around creators and helping drive  creation on the platform on the video  side we've got two initiatives one is  our amplify program and this is a  program for a premium content providers  to bring content on the platform and  share in revenue we now have over 225  television networks and premium content  providers doing this in 25 countries all  across the world we've begun to expand  this out to move beyond just premium  content providers to allow other  creators to upload video and share in  the revenue that we sell and then the  second thing we're doing is we have a  platform called niche which now has over  25,000 content provider or content  creators who use the platform and  essentially what it does is it helps  bring together advertisers with content  creators so content creators can provide  great content for those advertising  campaigns so we hear the rumors  constantly about twitter selling have  you considered selling have you gotten  offers the board has a fiduciary duty to  shareholders and I think you know from  the management teams perspective our  goal is to increase shareholder value  and we believe the roadmap that we have  ahead and the team that we have in place  is a strong team and we're continuing to  see growth LinkedIn is worth 50% of what  it was a week ago you're trying to turn  around a company  in an unforgiving market I mean is there  any part of you that thinks maybe this  would be easier or better if we were  private or if we were under someone  else's way look we don't even think  about that piece of it here's what we do  think about Twitter is a live platform  live is amazingly powerful for people  it's also amazingly powerful for the  business and it's our core strength you  see on the video side for example  products like periscope which we've now  integrated into Twitter are incredibly  compelling for both areas consumers and  the business side so I feel like we have  all of the right pieces in place the  business is growing and ultimately  consumer growth will be there as well  why not innovate faster or bigger like  why not just do do away with 140  character limit right now and see what  happens so we have started refining the  product in fact yesterday we turned on a  feature I encourage you and the people  at home I've seen it turn it on it's an  extension of our while you're away  feature which is if you haven't been to  Twitter for a while we bring the very  best tweets right to the top of your  timeline you simply pull your timeline  again and you go right back to live and  what's great about it is you know we  have over 300 million pieces of our  content creators on the platform who are  giving incredible insight and  information you think about you know  just what's happened over the last two  weeks for example in the political realm  politicians when they want to speak  directly to the world they do it on  Twitter first for the Super Bowl we had  players and journalists who were  communicating about the game and  actually a player who was at home who  decided to retire Marshawn Lynch just  through a tweet so I think you see  examples like that and you can't help  but think and know that Twitter is a  platform that is going to continue to to  really dominate Jack says his number one  priority is recruiting especially in the  executive ranks where are the holes what  are the gaps that you think need to be  filled well a baby or CLO yeah a big one  actually was on the marketing side  communicating the value of the company  to consumers in a stronger way was  definitely one of the priorities  Jack and I had over the summer as we  laid out the strategy for the company  I'm happy to say we've done that Leslie  Berlin who's an incredible executive  from American Express has just joined us  and actually started this week as our  chief marketing officer and she's going  to get right in right right to work to  help do that both on our performance ad  business and also for TV as well one  more question you're gonna like this one  you're known for being so nice in fact  recode actually turned that into a  headline but recently I've been seeing a  little bit more attitude  from Adam Bain when Wendy's and Burger  King had a smackdown on Twitter Facebook  said it happened on quote/unquote social  media and you weren't too happy with  that according to your tweets I love  Twitter and I want to make sure that  people understand the true power and  impact that it has in the world and it  is powerful are we gonna see being like  a little last night I can be a little  bit less nice all right Adam Bain CEO of  Twitter thank you so much for joining  thanks for having me

